.TH RAYJS 1
.SH NAME
rayjs, gemrun \- JavaScript graphics and a small 3D game
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rayjs
[
.B -m
.I megabytes
]
.I file.js
[
.I arg ...
]
.PP
.B games/gemrun
[
.B -a
]
[
.B -n
.I frames
]
[
.B -o
.I screenshot.png
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Rayjs
runs QuickJS with a statically linked
.B raylib
module for native window input, drawing and sound.
Graphics require a
.IR rio (4)
window and the VirGL stack described in
.IR gpu (3).
.PP
.B scriptArgs
contains the script path followed by its arguments.
.B print
writes arguments to standard output.
ES modules can import other JavaScript files by relative or absolute path.
Files ending in
.B .mjs
or containing module syntax are evaluated as modules;
other files are scripts.
.B -m
sets the JavaScript heap limit, in MiB (4 through 1024, default 128).
Native image, model and audio allocations are outside this limit.
.PP
The raylib module retains the C API's names and argument order.
Vectors are objects with
.B x,
.B y
and, for 3D,
.B z
fields; colors have integer
.B r,
.B g,
.B b,
.B a
fields in 0..255. Cameras have
.B position,
.B target,
.B up,
.B fovy
and
.B projection
fields. Numeric arguments must be finite numbers.
The standard raylib color constants have read-only components.
.PP
The supported calls are:
.IP
InitWindow, CloseWindow, WindowShouldClose, IsWindowReady,
EnableEventWaiting, DisableEventWaiting, SetTargetFPS, GetFrameTime, GetTime, GetFPS, GetScreenWidth, GetScreenHeight.
.IP
BeginDrawing, EndDrawing, ClearBackground, BeginMode3D, EndMode3D.
.IP
IsKeyDown, IsKeyPressed, IsKeyReleased, IsMouseButtonDown,
IsMouseButtonPressed, GetMouseX, GetMouseY, GetMouseWheelMove.
.IP
DrawText, DrawFPS, DrawRectangle, DrawCircle, DrawLine,
DrawCube, DrawCubeWires, DrawSphere, DrawPlane, DrawGrid.
.IP
LoadImage, LoadImageFromScreen, ExportImage, GenImageColor, GenImageChecked, UnloadImage,
LoadTexture, LoadTextureFromImage, UnloadTexture, DrawTextureEx,
LoadModel, UnloadModel, DrawModel.
.IP
InitAudioDevice, CloseAudioDevice, IsAudioDeviceReady,
LoadSound, LoadSoundFromWave, UnloadSound, PlaySound, StopSound,
IsSoundPlaying, SetSoundVolume.
.PP
Key constants cover arrows, Space, Enter, Escape and W, A, S, D, R, P.
Mouse constants cover the left, middle and right buttons.
Camera projections are CAMERA_PERSPECTIVE and CAMERA_ORTHOGRAPHIC.
.PP
Resource loaders return opaque objects. Images and textures expose read-only
.B width
and
.B height
properties. Unload calls are idempotent; other uses of unloaded resources
throw an exception. Garbage collection and process completion also release
resources. A model owns its imported material textures.
.PP
.B CloseWindow
releases its textures and models; reopening the window does not revive them.
.B CloseAudioDevice
releases all sounds. Images can outlive a window.
Drawing must be bracketed by BeginDrawing/EndDrawing;
3D drawing by BeginMode3D/EndMode3D inside a frame.
CloseWindow requires an ended frame.
.PP
LoadSoundFromWave accepts an object with integer
.B frameCount,
.B sampleRate,
.B sampleSize,
.B channels
and an
.B ArrayBuffer
in
.B data.
It copies the samples. Mono/stereo, 8-bit unsigned, 16-bit signed or 32-bit
floating PCM at 8000..192000 Hz is accepted; multibyte samples use native byte
order. Buffer length must match the format. Frame count is at most 2646000.
.PP
.I Gemrun
uses rayjs to collect eight gems while avoiding moving sentinels.
Arrows or WASD move, P pauses, R restarts, and Enter advances after a win.
Escape exits. Paused and finished games wait for input.
.B -a
enables synthesized sound,
.B -n
stops after a frame count, and
.B -o
saves the final image.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
import * as r from 'raylib';
r.InitWindow(640, 480, 'JavaScript');
r.SetTargetFPS(60);
while (!r.WindowShouldClose()) {
    r.BeginDrawing();
    r.ClearBackground(r.DARKBLUE);
    r.DrawText('hello', 20, 20, 24, r.WHITE);
    r.EndDrawing();
}
r.CloseWindow();
.EE
